Upon failure of \var{c0}, the system reconfigures by stopping the instance of planning software on \var{c1}, starting an instance of the vehicle interface software on \var{c1}, starting the Linux versions of the control and planning software on the laptop, making \var{c1} the primary replica for the perception software, and removing \var{c0} as a replica for the perception software (we continue to represent it as a replicated software instance, even though there is only one replica, so we can easily add a replica if \var{c0} recovers).

