In this experiment, we sampled 40K points for each mesh using Trimesh \cite{trimesh} API. We primarily utilize the Kaolin API \cite{jatavallabhula2019kaolin} to compute the values of SDF on octree grid points for the watertight surface in SE-RBFNet, while for non-watertight surfaces, we use the point-cloud-utils API \cite{point-cloud-utils}. Since the SparseRBF method generates extraneous surfaces in non-surface regions on some point clouds, which affects the clarity of the visual presentation, we manually remove these redundant surfaces during visualization. However, for quantitative evaluation, we still use the original reconstructed surface to compute the evaluation metrics.

