\subsubsection{Adaptive Resource Scheduling Algorithm} Aiming at the bursty traffic characteristics of trading systems, an adaptive resource scheduling algorithm based on deep
reinforcement learning was designed. The algorithm represents the system state as a vector $S=(C,M,N,L)$, where $C$ is the
CPU utilization, $M$ is the memory occupancy, $N$ is the network throughput, and $L$ is the load level. The action space $A$
includes container scaling, resource quota adjustment, and other operations. Through deep Q-network training, the
