Zero-touch networks have emerged as a key enabler of high-level automation in these industrial environments \cite{10004601}. By leveraging programmable interfaces and virtualization technologies (e.g., software-defined networking), zero-touch networks can proactively configure and optimize themselves with minimal or no human intervention \cite{9913206}. This end-to-end automation is especially vital in Industry 4.0 settings, where the diversity of IIoT devices, strict performance requirements, and rapid fluctuations in network demands render manual management impractical. Furthermore, the incorporation of machine learning (ML) into zero-touch networks allows data-driven decision-making that can accelerate response times and boost overall system efficiency \cite{10004601, 10004596}.

