satisfies that $\sigma_+(g) \subseteq P$ and $\sigma_-(g) \subseteq P^-$; however, $g^{-1}(\mathbb{R}_{<0})$ has two connected components. Figure \ref{FIG4}(c),(d) displays $\sigma(g)$ and $g^{-1}(\mathbb{R}_{<0})$.
\end{ex}

