\[ f_1(x_1) = x_1^{4} - 16 \, x_1^{3} + 83 \, x_1^{2} - 164 \, x_1 + 96, \quad f_2(x_1) = x_1^{2} - 10 \, x_1 + 20, \quad f(x_1,x_2) = f_1(x_1) + x_2 f_2(x_1).\]
The exponent vectors of $f$ and its Newton polytope is shown in Figure \ref{FIG4_new}(a). The sets $W_0, W_1, W_2$ from the proof of Proposition \ref{Thm_ParallelFaces} have the form
