\subsection{LLM Steering}

In this work, we adopt \textit{steering} as our jailbreak strategy due to its controbillity and without any dependence on auxiliary attacker models~\citep{chao2023jailbreaking,mehrotra2024tree}.

We initiate the jailbreak by directly manipulating the activations of the model’s internal layers in a targeted manner~\citep{kim2025linear}. Specifically, for each input prompt $\mathbf{x}_d$ (ie., excluding the response $\mathbf{y}_d$), we extract the attention activations $\mathbf{A} = \{\mathbf{a}_d^{l,h}\}$ from the self-attention modules of the target LLM $\mathbf{f}$, across every layer $l$ and head $h$.

\noindent \textbf{Probe Training.}  
Given these set of activations $\{\mathbf{a}_d^{l,h}\}$ and the corresponding jailbreak labels $y_d$ obtained from privacy evaluator, we train a linear probe model $w_d^{l,h}$ independently for each attention head activations $\mathbf{a}_d^{l,h}$. Each probe is trained on a balanced dataset: label $\mathbf{1}$ is assigned to \textit{refused} prompts, and label $\mathbf{0}$ to \textit{disclosed} prompts. For instance, the LLaMA-7B~\citep{touvron2023llama} contains $32$ layers with $32$ heads each, resulting in 1024 total probes. For our experiments, we use a balanced dataset of $112$ subjects ($56$ per class), with a $50/50$ train-validation split.

\noindent \textbf{Intervention.}  
We select the top-$k$ attention heads based on F1-score performance on the validation set. For the remaining evaluation subjects with label other than \textit{declosed} response label (denoted as $D_{test}$), we perform a steering intervention by modifying the activation of the last token at every time-step as follows:

\begin{equation}
\mathbf{a}_d^{l,h} = a_d^{l,h} + \alpha  w
\end{equation}\label{eq:eq1}

where $\alpha$ is a tunable scaling coefficient, and $w^{l,h}$ is the learned probe weight vector of the corresponding probe model. Finally, as in previous steps, we evaluate the response content after steering with the privacy evaluator and further verify the factuality of the response information using GPT-4~\citep{openai2023gpt}.




