Then, for $d \leq 5$, $Q_1$ and $Q_2$ can end up at a distance less than $d$, while $P_1$ and $P_2$ are at a distance at least $d$. Since there is a priori no way of ``distinguishing'' these two cases, we have to take $d$ ``large enough''. The precise argument appears in the proof of~\Cref{lem:dist-amiablefam}, Claim (\ref{clm:damiabilityP3}).

