Here, we have
the fixed extra cost of copying into the OS cache.
Hence,
the pattern of IO costs is similar to the direct IO
(\cref{fig:gplot_direct_cost}) with a minor extra overhead.
The copying overhead is negligible compared to the system call cost and
hence is hardly visible on \cref{fig:gplot_sync_cost}. But
it is observable in \cref{fig:sync_cost_range}, which compares the models
with the costs of writing data chunks of different sizes
