For non-synchronized IO with system calls, the OS caches the data before writing it to the storage
device.
\Cref{sec:mod-nonsync} discussed the effects of $\bgrate$ and $\dirtyratio$.
Here, we evaluate the model in two cases of $\dirtyratio=40\,\%$
(host 1) and $\dirtyratio = 20\,\%$ (host 2).
\Cref{fig:async_cost}-A compares the measured
non-sync IO costs with the model values of CAWL and SimGrid for
