	FMLP-L has the lowest overheads, due to the simplest mechanism. Overall, the overheads for all the protocols are relatively low and acceptable.
	For distributed-based protocols, we can observe that there are quite a few outliers. In fact, a similar observation has been reported in~\cite{shi-OSPERT17}. One reason could be that the behavior of cache memories kicks in to introduced operation overheads, but we have no sufficient data to pinpoint the exact cause here.

