    Let $k\leq n'/2$. Consider the \SMS with the aging strategy and with population size $\mu \geq \overline{M}+1+\tau$ optimizing $\mojzj$ starting with a population that covers $K_{m,k}$. Let $T$ denote the number of iterations until the population covers $C_{m,k}$ and let
    \begin{align*}
        t = &\left(1+\frac{\ln(4)m'+\ln(n)}{\ln(m')}\right)\frac{\ln(m')k\tau}{2}\\
        &\cdot\left(\frac{e^2 n}{k\left(1-\exp{\left(-\frac{\tau}{\mu}\right)}\right)}\right)^k .
    \end{align*}
    Then $T\leq t $ with probability at least $1-\frac{1}{n}$. Further, 
