\section{Experimental Setup}

Here we describe our experimental design to address the above research questions. All of our prompts, data collection scripts, and final results are made available as supplemental material online.

While one should strive to conduct experiments using only open source models, at the time of writing there are few high-quality open source models which support multiple images as input. 
As our research questions require pairs of images to be addressed, we are limited in our choice of models. %After careful discussion with subject matter experts (a subset of this work's authors), 
Although there are many LLM models, we chose to use OpenAI's ~\chatgpt (gpt-4o-2024-08-06) and Google's ~\gemini (gemini-2.5-pro-exp-03-25) models which are the state-of-the-art models in visual perception benchmarks\cite{chen2024we, lu2024wildvision} and easy to adopt.
%both of which are multimodal LLMs. 
Both models support API requests, allowing a larger-scale experiment such as ours to be conducted in a controlled environment. Additionally, the wide popularity of both models with the general public gives our experiment more external validity. 
