\section{Conclusions}
We investigate a topical question in visualization: ``Do MLLMs have the perceptual capacity to understand complex visualizations?'' We attempt to answer this question by replicating a recent human-subject study on a high-level perception task for node-link diagrams, using MLLMs. Our findings indicate that MLLMs achieve results comparable to human performance, and 
%though the amount of context given to the model affects the performance, with more context increasing performance. 
by carefully tuning the prompts, MLLMs can outperform humans. %better-than-human expert accuracy can be achieved for all but one group of instances. 
Reasoning responses given by MLLMs provide some insight into the underlying decision processes, including evidence that they use visual proxies similar to those used by humans.
